Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::bringing_a_card_up_is_total_against_any_controller`.

The defect: the SD power-up deadline subtracts the start time without wrapping, so a clock that
wraps past 2^64 during the second of power-up panics the driver.

Expected to fail: the subtraction overflow check in `sd_power_up`, which is the property the
harness states (the bring-up panics nowhere).
diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
@@ -444,7 +444,7 @@
         if operation_conditions & OPERATION_CONDITIONS_BUSY_DONE != 0 {
             return Ok(operation_conditions);
         }
-        if host.registers_mut().now_microseconds().wrapping_sub(start)
+        if host.registers_mut().now_microseconds() - start
             > POWER_UP_DEADLINE_MICROSECONDS
         {
             return Err(InitializationError::PowerUp(operation_conditions));
